infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title What keeps a narrowing — and what throws it away
  desc Narrowing holds on a straight, const-anchored path; a closure, await, or call between guard and use re-widens to the declared type
  compares
    - label Narrowing survives
      children
        - label Straight-line code after a guard
          desc Same uninterrupted control-flow path keeps the narrowed type
        - label const capture before the boundary
          desc const sid = id while id is string; const cannot be reassigned
        - label const keeps the literal
          desc const dir = up is type up, a usable discriminant
        - label Early return inside a guard
          desc Subtracts the handled type, narrowing the rest of the function
    - label Narrowing is discarded
      children
        - label Closure runs later
          desc setTimeout callback re-widens id to string or number
        - label await suspends and resumes
          desc Control left the function, so it restores string or null
        - label Call between guard and use
          desc Checker cannot prove the binding was not mutated
        - label let widens the literal
          desc let dir = up is string; the discriminant stops narrowing
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
